# Intent: a control panel that drops from the top of the screen (owner request 2026-10-21). A swipe down that begins in the top 30 px opens a sheet with the volume and brightness sliders and a Wi-Fi button (the saved-networks list from 036); a swipe down anywhere else still stops talking, and a swipe up no longer opens anything. The sheet closes on a swipe up, a tap outside it, or 5 s without touch (20 s on the Wi-Fi list). Letting go of a slider, or a left or right volume swipe, queues one level_changed event {volume, brightness} (patch 021's queue) so the host keeps its stored owner levels in step; a pending level_changed is replaced, never stacked.
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc, stackchan_display.h, hal/hal_mcp.cpp (MIT); new file hal/device_events.h. Applies after 044 with --unidiff-zero.
# Check after a flash: swipe down from the very top edge shows the sheet with both sliders at the current levels; dragging changes the level live; about 2 s after release the host's owner_levels.json holds the new level; 5 s without touch closes it (a drag keeps it open); tap outside and swipe up close it; the Wi-Fi button opens the list; a swipe down through the middle of the face while it speaks stops it and shows no sheet.
